We initialize the union-find data structure with N+1 elements, where N is the number of employees, and keep track of the indices being used for the union-find trees. If the union operation involves the same element, the result will be `n`, and if not, it will be `same_as_index(n)`. The `same_as_index()` function works within the given constraints.

In the reasoning phase, we need to inspect whether we have the correct answer by setting up a scenario where all given pairs of employees belong to the same departments. If this is not the case, we continue the reduction algorithm until we correctly recover the structure.

